========================================================================
F1 — CRITICAL — mode double-decoy (static redefinition)
========================================================================
STATUS: FIXED (this peer)

Evidence (pre-fix drive in c_emit.oo ~L165-169):
  if meta_layout {
      if mode != "preamble" && mode != "preamble_noarc" {
          c_emit_meta_decoy(meta_idx);
          meta_idx = meta_idx + 1;
      }
  }

Product multi-pass (cli_emit.oo L56-60; cli_build.oo emit-protos then
emit-bodies) invokes c_emit_stream_mode twice on the same src:
  1) mode=protos  → emits static void __oo_meta_decoy_0..N-1
  2) mode=bodies  → emits static void __oo_meta_decoy_0..N-1 AGAIN
meta_idx resets to 0 each call → identical symbols in one TU.

C result: redefinition of static function → compile fail for any
// METAMORPHIC: path-a source under default emit-c / product build.

Also: pure protos-only emit polluted .text with decoy *definitions*
after prototypes (wrong placement for "layout after fn bodies").

Fix:
  c_meta_layout_emit_decoys(mode) returns true only for:
    bodies | bodies_noarc | all | all_noarc | full
  false for protos | protos_noarc | preamble | preamble_noarc | unknown
  c_emit.oo: meta_emit = meta_layout && c_meta_layout_emit_decoys(mode);
  banner + per-fn decoy both gated on meta_emit.

Post-fix multi-pass: protos = no decoys; bodies = decoys once. Single-pass
all/full (EMIT_NO_CONCAT emit-c) still gets decoys once.

========================================================================
F2 — MEDIUM — protos-mode decoy emission (layout wrong pass)
========================================================================
STATUS: FIXED with F1

Pre-fix excluded only preamble*; protos still emitted full static
definitions. Couples to F1. After fix, protos emits zero decoys.

========================================================================
F3 — LOW — c_emit_meta_decoy missing negative-idx bounds
========================================================================
STATUS: FIXED

Pre-fix: idx.to_string() on negative → "__oo_meta_decoy_-1" which is not
a valid C identifier ('-' tokenizes as minus). Call site only increments
from 0, but API had no floor.

Fix: clamp safe < 0 → 0; refuse if id == "" (empty-name belt).

========================================================================
F4 — LOW — c_emit_meta_drive.oo missing / drive undisciplined
========================================================================
STATUS: OPEN residual (documented; not invented as new module)

Hunt asked for c_emit_meta_drive.oo — file does not exist. Drive logic was
inlined in c_emit_stream_mode without a mode allow-list (root cause of F1).
Peer hardened helpers in c_emit_meta.oo rather than adding a new drive
module (scope: fix meta / meta_drive only; no unsolicited new surface).

Residual: optional extract of drive loop to c_emit_meta_drive.oo later.

========================================================================
F5 — LOW — comment honesty "between" vs "after each"
========================================================================
STATUS: NOTED (header wording tightened in c_emit_meta.oo)

Pre-fix header: "between top-level fns". Implementation emits AFTER every
top-level fn including the last (N fns → N decoys). Correct for layout
diversity; wording was slightly misleading. Header now says "after each".

========================================================================
F6 — INFO/OK — parser bounds / infinite loop / off-by-one
========================================================================
STATUS: PASS (no defect)

c_parse_metamorphic_path_a:
  - loop: while i + nn <= sn; always i = i + 1 → terminates
  - char_at(src, i+j): j < nn ∧ i+nn <= sn ⇒ i+j < sn (no overflow read)
  - line-start: i==0 or char_at(src, i-1)=="\n"; never reads i-1 at 0
  - needle split ("// " + "METAMORPHIC: path-a") avoids self-host false
    enable if this module is ever path-a scanned as product src with a
    contiguous line-start needle in source text
  - empty src → false
  - leading-space line does not match (line-start only; matches MAX_CYCLES /
    SECRET directive style)

No infinite loop. No off-by-one on window end.

========================================================================
F7 — INFO/OK — empty decoy fn names
========================================================================
STATUS: PASS (post-guard)

Decoy symbol is always "__oo_meta_decoy_" + decimal digits after clamp.
Cannot emit empty function name. (User top-level empty IDENT in c_emit_fn
is out of scope — not produced by meta emitter.)

meta_idx only ++ from 0 in drive; no practical Int overflow for source-sized
fn counts. No upper cap added (not required for C id well-formedness).

========================================================================
NON-FINDINGS / RESIDUALS (honest, not counted as bugs)
========================================================================
- Full DESIGN runtime assembly mutation / ROP reshape: residual free-name
  refuse (metamorphic_emit / metamorphic_build) — by design, not a bug.
- meta_epoch process-local only (chs_rt_meta.c); not continuous re-morph.
- Unreferenced static decoys may be GC'd under -ffunction-sections
  --gc-sections; path-A layout diversity is best-effort at emit, not a
  link-forced keep. Residual product strength note.
- Live oodac binary on disk predates feature; smoke metamorphic_path_a_smoke.sh
  allows "skip live" when emit lacks decoys — source floor is the claim.
- c_emit.oo pre_pos / hitl_pre loops: separate; not meta bugs. If
  c_emit_fn_mode ever returned non-advancing pos, outer while would spin —
  pre-existing emit risk, not introduced by meta.

